  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe built-in Fanuc post (`assets/posts/fanuc.cps`) has two new options in the \"Smoothing\" group:\n\n- `aiContourControl` (boolean, default off): AI contour control (G05.1).\n- `aiContourLevel` (integer 1-10, default 5): the R word of `G05.1 Q1`.\n\nWith the option on, each operation writes `G05.1 Q1 R<level>` as the last preamble block. That is after `T M6`, `G43 H`, `S M3`, the coolant word and any `G68`. Each operation writes `G05.1 Q0` at its end. That is after `G80`, before `G69`, `M9` and `M5`.\n\nGuards:\n\n- A canned cycle writes `G05.1 Q0` before its cycle block. The Doosan DNM manual cited in `doosan-dnm.cps` requires Q0 before G73-G89.\n- A section with the spindle stopped (a touch probe with `G31`) does not arm AICC.\n- A level outside 1-10 is refused by name one time, and no `G05.1` is written. The host also refuses it from the declared range.\n- With the option on, the #616 note \"SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN\" is not written, because the post now writes the control's smoothing words.\n\nWith the option off (the default), the output does not change.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe machine owner (FANUC Robodrill, 31i-A5) uses AICC on each operation: \"G05.1 Q1 R5 in the start of op and then G05.1 Q0 at the end\". Before this change, the Fanuc post wrote only a comment for a Smoothing ask (#616), and it had no option for G05.1.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew file `crates/post/tests/fanuc_aicc.rs` (7 tests):\n\n- `fanuc_aicc_is_off_by_default`\n- `fanuc_aicc_on_brackets_each_operation`\n- `fanuc_aicc_level_is_the_option`\n- `fanuc_aicc_skips_a_probe_section`\n- `fanuc_aicc_level_out_of_range_is_refused_by_name`\n- `fanuc_aicc_on_replaces_the_smoothing_not_written_note`\n- `fanuc_aicc_options_are_declared_off_and_bounded`\n\nOn unchanged `fanuc.cps` (upstream/main), 5 of the 7 tests fail. The two tests that pass check that nothing is written (off by default, probe section).\n\nMutation results (each mutation fails its pin; restored, all 7 pass):\n\n- Remove `aiccOff()` before the canned cycle: `fanuc_aicc_on_brackets_each_operation` fails.\n- Remove the spindle and probe guard in `aiccOn()`: `fanuc_aicc_skips_a_probe_section` fails.\n- Remove the level range check: `fanuc_aicc_level_out_of_range_is_refused_by_name` fails.\n- Remove the early return in `smoothOn()`: `fanuc_aicc_on_replaces_the_smoothing_not_written_note` fails.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The option is off by default.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No program with the option on was run on a real control. The owner gave the block form. The placement before the first move and the Q0 before canned cycles are not confirmed on the 31i-A5.\n- Questions 1 and 2 of the issue (M29 before G84, G73 or G83, the R plane) are still open. The owner has not answered them. This PR does not change them.\n- The UI shows the new options through the generic declared-options page. No UI test was added.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/2603-fanuc-aicc.md`.\n\nChangelog: Fanuc post: new off-by-default option \"AI contour control (G05.1)\" writes `G05.1 Q1 R<level>` at each operation start and `G05.1 Q0` at its end (level 1-10, default 5).\n\nRefs #2603\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
